<http://data.silknow.org/object/8bfdc0e6-307f-36b8-9e47-b9844f52033b>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Beatrix Potter found some of the inspiration for her book <i>The Tailor of Gloucester</i> at the South Kensington Museum (now the V&A). She told her editor, Norman Warne, 'I have been delighted to find I may draw some most beautiful 18th century clothes at S. Kensington museum'. (from Sue Prichard's Access to Images entry for 652A-1898)"@en , "Rich blue silk coat with cutaway fronts, embroidered with sprays of stylised flowers and leaves in yellow, green, pink and cream silk. At the very edge is a simple border of leaves and sprigs. The embroidery is at the collar, closing edges, cuffs, pocket-flaps and coat tails. There are six embroidered buttons on the proper right front, three under either pocket-flap, three at the back-waist. The body is lined with cream linen and silk with twentieth-century repairs."@en , "Unique"@en , "Men's dress coat, embroidered, ca.1790 - ca.1800, England; Beatrix Potter, Tailor of Gloucester"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b508a67b-442f-3106-9c41-d3b1b2bfd6a0> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/2631a14f-b94c-3f35-a3bf-27a845d8dcd5> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c35c6133-6323-3979-abb2-e67159e5a9a0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Men's dress coat, embroidered, ca.1790 - ca.1800, England; Beatrix Potter, Tailor of Gloucester"@en , "Rich blue silk coat with cutaway fronts, embroidered with sprays of stylised flowers and leaves in yellow, green, pink and cream silk. At the very edge is a simple border of leaves and sprigs. The embroidery is at the collar, closing edges, cuffs, pocket-flaps and coat tails. There are six embroidered buttons on the proper right front, three under either pocket-flap, three at the back-waist. The body is lined with cream linen and silk with twentieth-century repairs."@en , "Unique"@en , "Beatrix Potter found some of the inspiration for her book <i>The Tailor of Gloucester</i> at the South Kensington Museum (now the V&A). She told her editor, Norman Warne, 'I have been delighted to find I may draw some most beautiful 18th century clothes at S. Kensington museum'. (from Sue Prichard's Access to Images entry for 652A-1898)"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/8bfdc0e6-307f-36b8-9e47-b9844f52033b/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/8bfdc0e6-307f-36b8-9e47-b9844f52033b/dimension/2> ;
